      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5e44a1bd0c91c2477a8b8acb|full_name}: I did see this! I use this personally for my animator when Grounded, yet this still affects my animator for mid air. I can kinda get around this when users are in SDK2 worlds and I check for if the VelocityX and VelocityZ are approximately 0, but SDK3 worlds still cause the user to walk on air or play the falling animation should one be provided until some force acts on them.\n\nVelocityMagnitude does hit 0 faster than VelocityX and VelocityZ, but isn't exactly Input strength as far as I can see",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
