  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-07-09T03:24:14.789Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Because of the nature of SDK3 worlds where the client's momentum is kept whenever they release their input bindings until friction acts upon them, unlike SDK2 worlds, animators which use the velocityX or Z parameters for locomotion based animations encounter the issue that they do not stop when they are supposed to which causes the user to walk on air or anything else that depends on input will not stop until the velocity is approximately 0. SDK2 avatars already have something similar and locomotion transitions are more instant which is more desirable in this case.",
